{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For he will turn away your son from after Me.</b> It did not say כי תסיר את בנך, and our Rabbis of blessed memory derived from here: 'Your daughter you shall not give to his son, and his daughter you shall not take for your son — כי יסיר את בנך מאחרי — your daughter's son who comes from the Cuthean is called your son, but your son who comes from the Cuthean woman is not called your son but her son.' The Torah's view in this is that the mother is the determining factor. And the explanation of the verse: when the Cuthean's son marries your daughter, he will turn away your son — the son your daughter will bear him — מאחרי, from after Me, for he will raise him from his youth to idolatry."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:16.188329361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}